findings.body:
`isProvisionedPromRule(promRule)` is defined as:

```
export function isProvisionedPromRule(promRule: PromRuleDTO): boolean {
  return prometheusRuleType.grafana.rule(promRule) && Boolean(promRule.provenance);
}
```

When passed a Cloud/Mimir `PromRuleDTO` (which has no `folderUid`/`uid`, hence `prometheusRuleType.grafana.rule` returns false), the function returns the falsy `false` rather than `false` via the type guard - that is fine, but it can be misleading because a missing `provenance` for a non-Grafana rule will return `false` as expected, yet a missing `provenance` for a Grafana rule returns `false` without distinguishing between 'not provisioned' and 'rule is not Grafana at all'. More importantly, the consumer `getIsProvisioned` in `RuleActionsButtons.V2.tsx` calls this even when the caller has not verified the rule is a Grafana rule; if a future caller passes a non-Grafana `promRule` (e.g. Mimir) the function silently returns false without indicating the rule was unhandled. Not a hard bug today, but worth flagging because the silent-false contract differs from `isProvisionedRule` (which type-narrows via `isGrafanaRulerRule`).
